// Low-level pixel access. px_idx maps (x, y) to a buffer offset; lset is the
// "store into a list element" helper (an imported list can't be index-assigned
// directly, but passing it as a parameter makes the lvalue an identifier again,
// and lists are reference-semantic so the store is shared) -- the same trick the
// engine uses for its screen buffer. Out-of-range writes are dropped by the
// runtime, so callers need no bounds check here.

lset(int[] xs, int i, int v) {
  xs[i] = v;
} return void;

px_idx(int x, int y) {
} return int y * (import gw) + x;

pset(int x, int y, int c) {
  lset((import fb), px_idx(x, y), c);
} return void;
